why Every Alliance quest of the Stockade in one run, lead-ins included.

# The Stockade's Alliance quests in one guide: Motley Garmason's Dark Iron
# War in the Wetlands, the pick-ups in Stormwind, Redridge and Duskwood, one
# run through the prison, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed
# over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The quests: Motley Garmason's 303 The Dark Iron War -> 378 The Fury Runs
# Deep (Kam Deepfury's head); Warden Thelwater's 387 Quell the Uprising;
# Nikova Raskol's 388 The Color of Blood (ten Red Wool Bandanas); Guard
# Berton's 386 What Comes Around... (Targorr's head); Councilman Millstipe's
# 377 Crime and Punishment (Dextren Ward's hand). For characters who handed
# in The Unsent Letter (373, from VanCleef in the Deadmines; the Deadmines
# guide takes it): Baros Alexston's 389 Bazil Thredd -> Thelwater's 391 The
# Stockade Riots (Bazil Thredd's head) -> 392 The Curious Visitor, back to
# Baros.
#
# Left out: none of the Alliance's. The Stockade is a city dungeon of the
# Alliance (its door is in Stormwind), so the pack has no Horde guide for it.
# The Bazil Thredd chain's steps apply only once The Unsent Letter is handed
# in, since it starts in the Deadmines.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses inside, so their goals stand
# at the door (@52.4,70.0, Stormwind; Forever's map frame, hence `coords
# live`) with `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon
# journal (Targorr the Dread, Kam Deepfury, Hamhock, Dextren Ward, Bazil
# Thredd; Bruegal Ironknuckle a rare), not of a recorded run. Every quest goal
# is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes them in another order
# still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items and rewards: Polestar's reference data (data/forever,
#   built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's Codex page for
#   the dungeon. The Dark Irons of Dun Modr are level 27 to 31, so that step
#   waits for 30.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   24 to 32).

